1 on PS1; CI running on PS2. New binding_recovery.py 411 LOC; binding_store.py 561 -> 530; binding_lifecycle.py 535 (docstring only).\n\nORDERING CORRECTION MADE BEFORE EARNING THE ATTESTATION. The story plan and this task's original impact set named run_differs.py as the invocation file for S3 T2, and the epic's constraint list asked for recovery \"after configuration snapshot/preflight ... but before remote issue fetch\". Verified against the spine: reconcile._load_snapshots (called at reconcile.py:222) constructs the store (:280), runs the under-lock staleness gate (:281-282), and performs the FIRST remote fetch (:328-333), while bind_operation_runtime is composed at :227 — AFTER _load_snapshots returns, hence after that fetch — and run_differs() is invoked at :231, also after it. So the requested conjunction is an EMPTY window, and no point inside run_differs.py can precede remote observation. Pre-observation is the load-bearing half (its purpose is to stop a pass interleaving new liveness evidence with completion), so the snapshot conjunct was dropped and the invocation moves to reconcile.py. Corrected the story plan + file_impact FIRST, then ran review-plan: PASS, signed, 0 blocking. The real size constraint is therefore reconcile.py at 795/800 — FIVE lines — not run_differs.py's 61.\n\nHELD-OUT TDD. 42 oracles authored RED-first against a signature-only scaffold; a bare ImportError was rejected as invalid RED, so the scaffold carries real signatures and the RED is 35 NotImplementedError failures with 6 correctly-green characterization/guard tests. The implementer saw 16; 26 discriminators were held outside the worktree and ALL passed unseen — the eight-case mismatch table, the write-counting idempotency oracles, replace-failure rollback, corrupt-retired fail-open, and tombstone authority against clear_absent and a same-key confirm. Implementer: 1 attempt per part, green first run.\n\nMUTATION FOUND ONE REAL ORACLE GAP, the same shape as S2 T1's and the fourth of this epic: replacing the targeted reverse pop with a SWEEP keyed on local_id stayed GREEN across all 41 tests, because every fixture had exactly one reverse key per local id. Closed with an out-of-band reverse orphan the forward entry never named — a targeted pop leaves it, a sweep takes it. Pinning the orphan's SURVIVAL is characterization not endorsement: no one-to-one forward/reverse invariant is claimed, which is why unbind carries its own orphan sweep and why bridge fsck reports reverse_missing_forward. All 8 seeded mutations now RED (rule-1 silence, dropped reverse-mismatch check, unconditional save, tombstone consumption, missing rollback, the sweep, check reordering, classifier impurity).\n\nTHE IMPLEMENTER FOUND A GENUINE TEST DEFECT AND REFUSED TO EDIT IT, correctly. test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py asserts the colon-form label by grepping SOURCE TEXT keyed on FILE NAME, and its own docstring named \"binding_store.py:706 (pending-binding recovery)\" as the third writer — so any faithful implementation of this move fails it. I retargeted the census to binding_recovery.py myself (I own the tests), verified by grep that exactly three production writers of f\"rebar-id:{local_id}\" remain and no hyphen-form write exists anywhere, and dropped the already-stale per-writer line numbers rather than refreshing them.\n\nTWO FALSE DOCSTRINGS CORRECTED: binding_lifecycle claimed recovery \"stays with BindingStore\", and the census above. TWO BEHAVIOURS PINNED AS THEY REALLY ARE against wording implying otherwise: a corrupt LIVE store cannot yield a safety abort (it fails CLOSED in the loader, so construction raises and repair is unreachable — the reachable corrupt-live case is a malformed ENTRY SHAPE, which parses and does reach the classifier); a corrupt RETIRED file fails OPEN, so tombstones go invisible and yield no candidate, making the consequence a missed repair rather than a guessed deletion.\n\nTHREE LLM-REVIEW ADVISORIES APPLIED, not deferred, all strengthening oracles: the replace-failure evidence carried repr(exc) that no test read (now pinned to the fault text, not just the category); the facade's three grace/age aliases had nothing holding them to the recovery module's objects, so a copy could let is_keyless_pending_within_grace and the unbind conjunction drift apart silently (identity test added); and the source-grep census now cross-references its behavioural twin. Both new assertions mutation-verified RED.\n\nPROCESS. Rebased onto origin/main d361eb28e4 (RP-04 C3a-CORE) with one conflict, in generated docs/env-vars.md, resolved by taking main's copy and regenerating. That file went stale AGAIN from a two-line docstring shift moving binding_lifecycle's non-literal env read 70 -> 72 — third time in this epic, caught pre-push by the checklist this time. rebar review-code still cannot preview locally: it returns runner \"code-review-disabled\" because verify.enable_code_review is off and there is no env override, so the surface-parity census in the commit message remains the mitigation. Commit-msg hook also enforces a 50-char subject, not just the 72-column body.\n\nGATES: 3373 passed / 9 skipped (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler + tests/interfaces/store + the comment-hygiene guard); 11671 passed / 53 skipped across the whole tests/unit tree pre-rebase; lint clean, mypy 567 files, complexity new=0 increased=0, comment hygiene, config ownership, verify-gate parity, config-check all green.\n\nDEFECT FILED: easygoing-tremendous-frogmouth (7851-e06b-9e85-4c9e) discovered_from the S3 story — preview and dry-run passes perform remote add_label/set_entity_property writes during create recovery, because that call's only guard is `if not scoped_ids` and it is handed the real configured transport, while the invariant-filing gate immediately beside it composes both axes. This task's AC6 pins that gate unchanged rather than fixing it.","timestamp":1787142033308912001}],"created_at":1787027651760140001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6a95e58f-3917-42d7-a54d-7a873f1f6fa4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"350a-0dc3-37e3-4089"},{"link_uuid":"89508b23-d70b-42ae-93dc-11756ea9cf86","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7efc-8fd1-1a49-4214"}],"description":"## Context\nCurrent recovery handles interrupted creates but not the retired-first/live-replace crash state where one exact identity remains both live and tombstoned. Recovery must never guess across mismatched identities.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract create recovery and add a pure interrupted-retirement classifier plus repository-backed completion operation behind the `BindingStore` facade. Do not invoke it automatically yet.\n\n## Plan\n1. Move keyed/keyless create recovery into `binding_recovery.py` without changing labels, immutable known-key behavior, three-miss plus 3600-second grace, failure tally, or continue behavior. Keep the facade's `recover_pending_bindings` signature and return value so the existing `run_differs.py` call site is untouched.\n2. Build real fault-cut fixtures for a tombstone persisted before live replacement fails.\n3. Classify retirement completion only when the tombstone, the live forward entry, and the live reverse entry agree on exact local id and Jira key.\n4. Complete by removing the redundant live forward/reverse pair while retaining the tombstone; repeat is a no-op. Mismatch, corruption, or replace failure safety-aborts and retains evidence.\n\n## Testing\nUse fresh store reloads, identity-mismatch tables, replacement cuts, and keyed/keyless create-recovery regressions. The existing create-recovery suites (`test_write_ahead_recovery.py`, `test_recovery_loud_failures.py`, `test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py`, `test_identity_write_retention_heldout.py`) are the extraction's regression oracle and must pass unmodified; new tests add a direct-module tier rather than duplicating them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Exact tombstone/forward/reverse overlap completes to coherent retired-only bytes while retaining the tombstone.\n- [x] Repeating completion performs no write.\n- [x] Any identity mismatch, corrupt live file, or replace failure retains evidence and returns a typed safety abort.\n- [x] Keyed pending recovery performs no search.\n- [x] Keyless pending recovery still requires both three misses and 3600 seconds, and one entry failure does not stop others.\n- [x] The pre-existing create-recovery invocation gate is behaviorally unchanged by this move: it stays UNSCOPED-passes-only (guarded solely by `if not scoped_ids`) with no write-bearing/persist gate, and no new write-bearing or scope condition is attached to it.\n\n## Out of scope\nAutomatic invocation boundary for retirement completion, rich-emission caller cutover, and ADR finalization.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_recovery.py","reason":"New owner: create recovery plus the exact-match retirement classifier and completion."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Expose compatible recovery delegates through the facade and alias the moved grace constants."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"Correct the module docstring's now-false claim that recovery stays with BindingStore."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_recovery.py","reason":"Fault-cut, mismatch, idempotency, replace-failure, and tombstone-authority oracles."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py","reason":"Retarget the label-writer census, which is keyed on file name, to the moved recovery module."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py","reason":"Keyed/keyless create-recovery regression coverage."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","486a-69ef-6370-48ff"],["relates_to","350a-0dc3-37e3-4089"],["relates_to","7efc-8fd1-1a49-4214"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"486a-69ef-6370-48ff","parent_status_uuid":"be824d3d-ca28-4c51-aa75-b1f4d41e8a38","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp02","binding-recovery","tdd"],"ticket_id":"c4f7-82ff-1004-4da5","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S3 T1 — Classify and complete interrupted binding operations","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_recovery.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Exact retirement completion, repeat, mismatch safety, and keyed/keyless create recovery"}]},"source_event_uuids":["93a67061-edc1-462a-93a2-562da6d2b10d","44ce68e8-2387-4823-b12b-05596ac2d4bc","ae37ee85-4c38-48c1-978b-89f1e1b2e214","b0300131-31e7-4bd9-85bc-deb611926056","c5f77f1a-432e-43ae-9479-4f89e49d2012","90df6e3f-0ea0-4c54-8785-81439cec1dde","9ddea875-0af4-47c1-b9e5-db61297cea09","6a95e58f-3917-42d7-a54d-7a873f1f6fa4","bd5dc0a4-ee85-4b40-bcdd-ea4e459f70b9","89508b23-d70b-42ae-93dc-11756ea9cf86","1c5fabba-04f4-426e-84a5-c0904ed80f92","3c8249dc-b946-4daf-85d3-3f9f463fe6ac","be824d3d-ca28-4c51-aa75-b1f4d41e8a38","4ecf99cc-c129-4df9-8dce-29371441e5c0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787154618302640001,"uuid":"5f967c8a-b5f2-4d6d-9aa0-48ca7e230172"}